# Paracord Docker secrets — copy to .env and fill in before `docker compose up -d`.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `docker compose up` intentionally FAILS FAST until every secret below is set to
# a non-empty value (the compose file uses the ${VAR:?...} form). Each secret must
# be unique and random before you expose the stack to a network — the values here
# are BLANK on purpose so no shared/default secret ever ships.

# JWT signing secret for user sessions.
# generate: openssl rand -hex 32
PARACORD_JWT_SECRET=

# Shared LiveKit secret. The paracord and livekit services both read this same
# variable; the key id "paracordlocal" is not a secret and stays in the compose
# file. Anyone who knows this secret can forge LiveKit join tokens — keep it private.
# generate: openssl rand -hex 32
PARACORD_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
